LICENSE PLACEHOLDER

No license has been chosen for this project yet. Until one is added, the default legal position
is "all rights reserved": nobody else may legally use, copy or modify this code.

Decide before publishing, then replace this file with the full license text, and add the
`license` field to pyproject.toml.

Common options:

  MIT          Very permissive, short, widely understood. Allows commercial use and
               closed-source derivatives, requires keeping the copyright notice. Recommended
               for a library like this unless you have a specific reason otherwise.
  Apache-2.0   Permissive like MIT, plus an explicit patent grant. A good choice if patents
               or corporate contributors are a concern.
  GPL-3.0      Copyleft: derivatives must also be released under the GPL. Choose it if you
               want improvements to stay open.

The dataset is a creative and editorial work as well as code. If you want different terms for
it (for example CC BY 4.0), say so here when you decide.

